# --- environment (re-derivable; the venv is shared with research-scale-100k)
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- secrets: never commit
.env

# --- inputs (re-derivable: pairs in ~5 min with DuckDB)
data/pairs.parquet
data/stats/
data/duckdb_tmp/
data/chosen.parquet

# --- large intermediates, pushed as GitHub release assets instead
#     (see ARTIFACTS.md; every one is rebuilt by a documented command)
data/sent_sample_fp16.npy
data/sent_vi_fp16.npy
data/lgbm/

agent-work/

# NOTE: gitignore has no inline comments. A trailing "# ..." becomes part of the pattern,
# which silently stops it from matching. Comments go on their own line.

# Committed on purpose (evidence trail):
#   data/pairs_manifest.json   sha256, per-shard counts, split rule, exclusions
#   data/chosen_shard.json     which shard the coreset selected, and the four scores
#   data/map_*.npz             512x512 W + b, ~1 MB each: the fitted artefact
#   data/sent_sample_meta.parquet  row -> shard map for the released embedding asset
#   data/per_sent_*.npz        per-sentence errors used by the mining join
#   results/*.csv|json|jsonl   sweep, geometry, BLEU/chrF/COMET, LGBM-vs-ridge, coreset, mining
#   results/figures/*          every figure in the paper
#   adapters/                  LoRA adapters (~4 MB each)
#   *.ipynb                    executed in place; the outputs are the evidence
